ionTest.java with 5 unit tests covering Jackson date serialization.\nWhy: @JsonFormat defaults to UTC, but spec requires server timezone; ObjectMapper must call setTimeZone(TimeZone.getDefault()) to propagate local TZ to @JsonFormat patterns.\nDiscovered: jackson-databind 2.9.11.1 does not exist in Maven Central — corrected to 2.9.10.8. All subsequent items should use this version.\nDifficulty: S as planned, but timezone subtlety added ~10 min debugging.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:10:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 2 - Request/Response DTOs\nChanges: Created EmployeeRequest.java and ErrorResponse.java in com.example.legacy.dto. EmployeeRequest has 5 fields with validation annotations. ErrorResponse has status/message/timestamp fields plus nested FieldError inner class for validation error details.\nWhy: javax.validation 1.1.0.Final lacks @NotBlank and @Email; used org.hibernate.validator.constraints for those two. Standard javax.validation.constraints used for @NotNull, @Size, @DecimalMin.\nDiscovered: javax.validation 1.1 annotation gap — @NotBlank and @Email require Hibernate Validator's own constraints package in this stack.\nDifficulty: S as planned; 5 min to diagnose annotation package issue.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":3,"newStart":14,"newLines":10,"lines":[" Why: javax.validation 1.1.0.Final lacks @NotBlank and @Email; used org.hibernate.validator.constraints for those two. Standard javax.validation.constraints used for @NotNull, @Size, @DecimalMin."," Discovered: javax.validation 1.1 annotation gap — @NotBlank and @Email require Hibernate Validator's own constraints package in this stack."," Difficulty: S as planned; 5 min to diagnose annotation package issue.","+","+=== Session 2026-03-19T22:00:00+09:00 ===","+Completed: Item 3 - Database schema and test resources","+Changes: Created src/main/resources/schema.sql (PostgreSQL DDL with BIGSERIAL), src/test/resources/schema.sql (H2-compatible DDL with BIGINT AUTO_INCREMENT), src/test/resources/application-test.properties (H2 in-memory MODE=PostgreSQL config).","+Why: Used separate DDL files per profile instead of relying on H2 PostgreSQL mode to support BIGSERIAL — avoids runtime DDL failures and is more explicit. H2 test schema uses DROP TABLE IF EXISTS + CREATE TABLE (no IF NOT EXISTS) to ensure clean state per test run.","+Discovered: No new discoveries. Followed plan: BIGINT AUTO_INCREMENT for H2, BIGSERIAL for PostgreSQL, MODE=PostgreSQL in JDBC URL for H2 compatibility.","+Difficulty: S as planned."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
